  "text_pages": [
    "Visa & Immigration > Exchange Program | 중앙대학교 국제교류팀\nGlobal Gateway\nCAU\nExchange Program\nHOME\nExchange Program\n소개\n협정대학\nExchange Program\n파견 프로그램\nShort-Term Program\n단기 프로그램\nVisa & Immigration\nNotice\nOverview\nAdmission Procedures\nVisa & Immigration\nHousing & Life\nVisa & Immigration\n공유\nStudent Visa(D-2-6)\nStudents who have successfully completed the online application will receive their Certificate of Admission (COA) in January (Spring) or July (Fall). It is the student’s responsibility to use the COA to apply for and obtain a D-2-6 Student Visa, which is required to study at Chung-Ang University. The student visa must be applied for at a Korean Embassy or Consulate.\nPlease note that the D-2 visa is a single-entry visa. Once you enter Korea using the D-2 visa, you are not permitted to leave the country until you have completed Alien Registration. Failure to complete Alien Registration before departure may result in immigration-related issues.\nFor more information, please refer to the\nfact sheet\nRequired Documents\nVisa application form (Download at\nHiKorea\n)\nPassport and a scanned copy of the passport\nPassport sized photo (3.5cm×4.5cm with white background; must be taken within the past 6 months)\nCertificate of Admission (표준입학허가서; issued by CAU)\nCAU Business Registration (사업자등록증; issued by CAU)\nApplication fee\nOriginal copy of documents proving financial ability (when submitting a parent's bank statement, family relation certificate is required to submit)\nLetter of Recommendation issued by home university\nDocument of proof for the participation of exchange student program (official document of the host university, exchange student agreement between universities)\nDocument of proof for the enrollment of the student at home university Additional documents may be required depending on the embassy or consulate.\nInformation on Visa\nHiKorea\nKorea Visa Portal\nStudents who do not hold a valid D-2-6 Student Visa (e.g., those who enter Korea on a C-type or H-type visa) are not permitted to study as an Exchange/Visiting Student at CAU. If such a case is identified, the student’s participation in the Exchange/Visiting Student Program will be cancelled.\nExtension of Student Visa\nInternational students who have been approved of the extension of their stay at CAU by the OIA may apply for extension of their student visa 2 months before the expiration date. Students need to visit the Immigration Office in January (Spring) / July (Fall) with the required documents.\nRequired Documents\nVisa application form\nPassport and a scanned copy of the passport\nExtended Certificate of Admission (issued by CAU)\nFinancial Statement\nApplication fee\nTranscript of Records at Chung-Ang University\nAdditional documents may be required depending on the nationality/Immigration Office.\nResidence Card (Alien Registration)\nAll international students who will stay in Korea for more than 91 days are required to complete Alien Registration (Residence Card, RC) within 90 days of arrival.\nAs the D-2 visa is a single-entry visa, students are not permitted to leave Korea before completing the RC process. If a student exits Korea without completing Alien Registration, their participation in the Exchange/Visiting Student Program may be cancelled due to immigration regulations.\nThe OIA provides support for group RC applications at the beginning of the semester.\nRequired Documents\nApplication form\nScanned copy of the passport\nPassport sized photo (3.5cm×4.5cm with white background; must be taken within the past 6 months)\nApplication fee\nCertificate of Registration at Chung-Ang University (재학증명서)\nIt will take about 4-5 weeks to receive the Residence Card, which will act as the student’s ID card in Korea.\nExchange Program\nNotice\nOverview\nAdmission Procedures\nVisa & Immigration\nHousing & Life"
  ],
